From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <codex@project-luma.local>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 23:28:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] profile: accept 19-digit ICCID selectors

Operational eSIM profiles may expose either a 19- or 20-digit ICCID. Keep the
protected standard-input selector strict, but accept both standard lengths so
the caller does not have to fall back to an ISD-P AID that a given eUICC may
not accept for profile enablement.
---
 src/applet/profile/enable.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/applet/profile/enable.c b/src/applet/profile/enable.c
index 1919426..9c271bd 100644
--- a/src/applet/profile/enable.c
+++ b/src/applet/profile/enable.c
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ static char *read_profile_id(void) {
     id[strcspn(id, "\r\n")] = '\0';
     length = strlen(id);
 
-    if (length == 20) {
+    if (length == 19 || length == 20) {
         for (size_t i = 0; i < length; i++) {
             if (!isdigit((unsigned char)id[i])) {
                 secure_profile_id_free(&id);
-- 
2.51.0
